<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="2.0">
  <category><pattern>WHAT IS LEARN</pattern><template>&lt;learn&gt; teaches a new category at runtime for the current session. It is not saved to disk. Use &lt;learnf&gt; only with an interpreter-side persistence policy.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>LEARN</pattern><template><srai>WHAT IS LEARN</srai></template></category>
  <category><pattern>EXAMPLE LEARN</pattern><template>Try: teach me that test phrase means this is a test response. Then say test phrase.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME THAT * MEANS *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star index="1"/></pattern><template><star index="2"/></template></category></learn>TAUGHT_OK|<star index="1"/>|<star index="2"/></template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME A GREETING FOR *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star/></pattern><template>Hello from a freshly taught greeting.</template></category></learn>Taught "<star/>" as a greeting. Try it.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME THAT WHEN I SAY * YOU SAY *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star index="1"/></pattern><template><star index="2"/></template></category></learn>Rule learned. Pattern: <star index="1"/>. Response: <star index="2"/>.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME AN ECHO RULE FOR *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star/></pattern><template>Echo rule fired. You said the pattern that matched.</template></category></learn>Echo rule taught for "<star/>". Try it.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME THAT AFTER * I SAY * YOU SAY *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star index="2"/></pattern><that><star index="1"/></that><template><star index="3"/></template></category></learn>Learned a follow-up rule after "<star index="1"/>": "<star index="2"/>" to "<star index="3"/>".</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH CODER THAT * MEANS *</pattern><template><learn><topic name="coder"><category><pattern><star index="1"/></pattern><template><star index="2"/></template></category></topic></learn>Taught in coder topic: "<star index="1"/>" to "<star index="2"/>".</template></category>
  <category><pattern>TEACH ME TO REMEMBER * AS *</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern><star index="1"/></pattern><template><set name="taughtValue"><star index="2"/></set>Stored. Ask what did I teach you.</template></category></learn>Taught "<star index="1"/>" to store "<star index="2"/>".</template></category>
  <category><pattern>WHAT DID I TEACH YOU</pattern><template><condition name="taughtValue"><li value="">Nothing taught yet. Try: teach me to remember color as blue.</li><li>You taught me a value: <get name="taughtValue"/>.</li></condition></template></category>
  <category><pattern>RESET LEARNED</pattern><template><learn><category><pattern>RESET LEARNED</pattern><template>Nothing to reset. Learned categories are session-scoped.</template></category></learn>Learned rules are session-scoped. Restart the interpreter to clear them.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>FORGET *</pattern><template>Standard AIML has no portable forget tag. Learned categories remain until the session ends; restart the interpreter to clear them.</template></category>
  <category><pattern>*</pattern><template><condition name="mode"><li value="coder">Coder mode. Try teach coder that X means Y or what is learn.</li><li value="assistant">Assistant mode. Try teach me that X means Y or what is learn.</li><li>I do not have a rule for "<star/>" yet. You can teach me: teach me that your phrase means my response.</li></condition></template></category>
</aiml>
